description:
**HR Generalist — IBEES** 




**Location:** 
 On\-site (Delhi)




**Experience:** 
 6–8 years




**Industry:** 
 Brand Communication / Advertising / Digital \& Offline Marketing




**Employment Type:** 
 Full\-time




 IBEES is a brand communications agency offering integrated
 **offline and digital solutions** 
 . We are looking for a mature, hands\-on
 **HR Generalist** 
 who can independently manage the employee lifecycle while helping us strengthen recruitment, performance, learning, culture and people practices.




 This is not intended to be a purely administrative HR role. We are looking for someone who can combine
 **strong execution with sound HR judgement** 
 , work closely with business and creative teams, and build practical people processes suited to a fast\-moving agency environment.




**Key Responsibilities** 



* Own the
 **end\-to\-end recruitment process** 
 across creative, digital, client servicing, media, strategy, operations and support functions.
* Partner with department heads to understand manpower requirements, define role expectations, improve hiring quality and reduce time\-to\-fill.
* Build and maintain structured talent pipelines through job portals, referrals, networking and other relevant sourcing channels.
* Manage the complete
 **employee lifecycle** 
 including onboarding, confirmation, transfers, documentation, engagement, grievance handling and exits.
* Drive a structured
 **Performance Management System (PMS)** 
 including KRAs, KPIs, goal\-setting, review cycles, performance discussions, calibration and Performance Improvement Plans where required.
* Work with managers to improve the quality of performance conversations and ensure that appraisals are evidence\-based and aligned with business objectives.
* Identify capability gaps through
 **Training Needs Analysis** 
 and develop practical learning and development initiatives for employees and managers.
* Create and maintain an annual training calendar covering functional, behavioural, managerial and leadership development requirements.
* Build an engaging and accountable
 **company culture** 
 through employee communication, recognition, feedback mechanisms, engagement initiatives and manager sensitisation.
* Conduct employee pulse checks, one\-to\-one discussions, exit interviews and other feedback exercises to identify people issues early.
* Analyse attrition, absenteeism, hiring effectiveness, training effectiveness, employee engagement and other relevant HR metrics.
* Support payroll inputs, attendance, leave, benefits administration, statutory compliance and employee records in coordination with finance/accounts or external partners.
* Review and strengthen HR policies, SOPs, employee handbook practices and internal processes as the organisation grows.
* Maintain strong employee relations while handling grievances and sensitive matters with maturity, confidentiality and fairness.
* Build useful HR dashboards and MIS for management covering headcount, recruitment, attrition, performance, engagement and other key people metrics.
* Act as a trusted HR partner to management while remaining approachable and credible with employees.



**Recruitment Expectations** 




 The person should be comfortable hiring for a diverse agency workforce, which may include roles such as:




**Creative, Copywriting, Graphic Design, Digital Marketing, Performance Marketing, Social Media, Client Servicing, Media, Strategy, Content, Video, Business Development, Operations, Finance and Administration.** 




 Experience hiring for advertising, digital, media, communications, creative services, marketing or other fast\-paced service businesses would be an advantage.




**Performance Management** 




 A major part of this role will be strengthening the performance culture at IBEES. The candidate should be capable of:



* translating business objectives into departmental and individual KRAs;
* defining measurable KPIs;
* creating appraisal calendars and review processes;
* helping managers conduct meaningful reviews;
* driving mid\-year and annual performance discussions;
* managing rating calibration;
* identifying high performers and development needs;
* supporting PIPs for underperformance;
* connecting performance outcomes with development, recognition and career progression.



**Learning \& Development** 




 The HR Generalist will be expected to move beyond organising training programmes and develop a more structured learning framework.




 Responsibilities will include:



* Training Needs Analysis;
* competency\-gap identification;
* employee development plans;
* induction and orientation;
* functional and behavioural training;
* manager\-development programmes;
* external trainer/vendor coordination;
* training feedback and effectiveness measurement.



**Culture \& Employee Engagement** 




 IBEES is looking for someone who understands that
 **culture is more than events and celebrations** 
 .




 The role should help strengthen:



* accountability;
* collaboration;
* recognition;
* communication;
* trust;
* manager effectiveness;
* employee experience;
* ownership and performance orientation.



 Employee engagement programmes, town halls, recognition initiatives, feedback mechanisms and internal communication should support these larger cultural objectives.




**AI \& Technology Orientation — Added Advantage** 




 We would particularly value a candidate who is curious about technology and understands how
 **AI and automation can improve HR productivity and decision\-making** 
 .




 Hands\-on technical expertise is not mandatory, but the candidate should ideally be comfortable exploring tools for:



* AI\-assisted resume screening and sourcing;
* job\-description creation;
* interview\-question generation;
* candidate communication;
* onboarding automation;
* HR helpdesks/chatbots;
* employee surveys and sentiment analysis;
* HR dashboards and analytics;
* training\-content development;
* PMS tracking;
* workflow automation;
* HRMS and ATS platforms.



 Familiarity with tools such as
 **ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Gemini, Canva AI, HRMS/ATS systems, Excel/Google Sheets and automation platforms** 
 would be an advantage.




 Most importantly, the individual should understand that AI is a
 **productivity and decision\-support tool** 
 , while final HR decisions must remain thoughtful, fair and human\-led.




**Candidate Profile** 




 We are looking for someone with:



* **6–8 years of relevant HR experience** 
 ;
* strong hands\-on experience as an HR Generalist, HRBP, HR Manager or similar;
* proven recruitment capability;
* practical experience with PMS;
* exposure to employee engagement and culture\-building;
* experience in learning and development;
* strong employee\-relations and grievance\-handling capability;
* good understanding of HR operations and statutory compliance;
* strong written and verbal communication;
* confidence in dealing with senior management and department heads;
* good Excel/Google Sheets and HR reporting capability;
* ability to work independently and execute without excessive supervision.



 An
 **MBA/PGDM in HR or equivalent HR qualification** 
 would be preferred.




**Preferred Characteristics** 




 The ideal person will be:




**hands\-on, commercially aware, structured, approachable, assertive when necessary, data\-oriented, technology\-curious and comfortable working in a fast\-paced creative environment.** 




 They should be able to switch comfortably between:




**interviewing a candidate in the morning, resolving an employee issue, discussing KRAs with a department head, reviewing an HR dashboard and planning a training programme—all within the same day.** 




**What Success Looks Like in the First 6–12 Months** 




 A successful HR Generalist at IBEES should be able to demonstrate:



* improved recruitment turnaround and quality of hiring;
* a clearly defined PMS with measurable KRAs/KPIs;
* improved quality of manager\-employee performance discussions;
* a structured learning calendar;
* stronger onboarding;
* improved employee engagement and communication;
* reduced regrettable attrition;
* stronger HR documentation and process discipline;
* useful management dashboards;
* increased adoption of technology and AI for appropriate HR workflows.

**About Us**
 We are the independent expert in assurance and risk management. Driven by our purpose, to safeguard life, property, and the environment, we empower our customers and their stakeholders with facts and reliable insights so that critical decisions can be made with confidence.




 As a trusted voice for many of the world’s most successful organizations, we use our knowledge to advance safety and performance, set industry benchmarks, and inspire and invent solutions to tackle global transformations.




**About Business Assurance**
 We help companies ensure compliance, build high\-performing management systems, and meet competence needs within a wide range of industries. DNV helps companies understand Working with us, you can be involved in technically challenging and innovative projects worldwide demanding a broad variety of expertise. Our strong focus on research and innovation opens an array of opportunities, and allows you to engage in projects which develop next generation solutions. and manage their risk picture through our management system certification and training portfolios.




**About The Role**
 The Training Manager is responsible for leading training services technically and commercially by managing a team of people directly and indirectly. This position is a member of local unit management team to position and grow training services in line with DNV Business Assurance strategy. This position plays a key role in positioning DNV’s vision “To be a trusted partner in tackling global transformation” in the market and customers through enabling a team of sales and operation functions. This position is expected to translate DNV Business Assurance’s global strategy into actions in India market to help customers in navigating their sustainability journey through the application of internationally recognized standards.




 This is a leadership role with several people reporting to this position and be part of management team in DNV Business Assurance India. This position reports to the Area Manager, India and Middle East and will be part of the Business Assurance global Training network in DNV Business Assurance.




**Main Responsibilities**
* Understand DNV Business Assurance strategy for Growth, prepare and implement a strategy for training services in India aligned with global;
* Seek opportunities to develop new business and share relevant market knowledge with other stakeholders to ensure the opportunities are pursued;
* Develop and lead strategies to achieve business targets in training service in DNV India, including annual business plans, budgets, and forecasts for training service;
* Establish strategic partnerships with industry associations, educational institutions, and corporate organizations;
* Conduct market research to identify industry trends and customer training needs, including competitive landscape;
* Lead team to generate leads through networking, referrals, industry events, and digital platforms;
* Own and continuously develop the India training portfolio; Establish and maintain library of training courses including training catalogues, course materials;
* Liaising with DNV Global Training Office for new training courses and updates of existing courses;
* Lead and develop public training course offerings and execution together with Marketing and Communications function; Own Training offering (content, accuracy, etc) at the DNV website and other platforms.
* Manage execution of all trainings in line with DNV’s value proposition by maintaining competence management of trainers, including identification, qualification of trainers in all fields of training service;
* Drive capability\-building initiatives within the training function;
* Achieve Training service revenue annual budgets.
* Participate and contribute at the DNV global training network meetings, initiatives and ensure the sharing and implementation in India;
* Responsible for managing team performance through coaching, mentoring and competence development of the sales team in India;
* Working closely with team members to encourage collaboration internally and with other business area in order to achieve business results, growth and innovation;
* Take lead in developing new services with a clear project management approach to go to market as fast as possible;
* Lead, Coach and support the development and career growth of team members;


 What we offer




* Flexible work arrangements for better work\-life balance
* Generous Paid Leaves (Annual, Sick, Compassionate, Local Public, Marriage, Maternity, Paternity, Medical leave)
* Medical benefits ( Insurance and Annual Health Check\-up)
* Pension and Insurance Policies (Group Term Life Insurance, Group Personal Accident Insurance, Travel Insurance)
* Training and Development Assistance (Training Sponsorship, On\-The\-Job Training, Training Programme)
* Additional Benefits (Long Service Awards, Mobile Phone Reimbursement)
* Company bonus/Profit share.


 \*Benefits may vary based on position, tenure/contract/grade level\*




 DNV is an Equal Opportunity Employer and gives consideration for employment to qualified applicants without regard to gender, religion, race, national or ethnic origin, cultural background, social group, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, age or political opinion. Diversity is fundamental to our culture and we invite you to be part of this diversity.




**About You**
* Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Business, HR, or technical discipline; relevant L\&D certifications are a strong plus.
* Minimum 15\+ years in the field of management systems, with minimum 5 years experience of techno commercial management of training services in the role of training service governance and business development;
* Strong understanding of various management systems such as ISO 9001, 14001, 45001, 50001, etc., and audit methodologies
* Strategic approach towards customers and potential clients by translating knowledge and understanding in offering innovative and value\-added solutions;
* Market intelligence and in\-depth understanding of competitive landscape in India;
* Exposure to digital learning platform management, remote learning, eLearning methodologies;
* Experience in partnering with institutions, organizations, associations, platforms and other relevant bodies;
* Experience in managing and developing key accounts / customers and winning new clients;
* Strong interpersonal relationship\-building capability to manage the team locally and remotely;
* Collaboration skills in working with cross functional teams locally and globally in different functions;
* Leadership skills such as mentoring, coaching, and developing people;
* Strong analytical skills to interpret mega and mini trends in market, internal process metrics;
* Objective decision making using sound and relevant data and benchmarks.


*Security and compliance with statutory requirements in the countries in which we operate is essential for DNV. Background checks will be conducted on all final candidates as part of the offer process, in accordance with applicable country\-specific laws and practices.*

**Your role, your impact**
 As a Functional Analyst within the Oracle ERP \& HCM Center of Excellence (CoE) , you’ll play a critical role in supporting, optimizing, stabilizing, and continuously improving Oracle Fusion Human Capital Management (HCM) solutions within an internal ERP Center of Excellence. You’ll work closely with Human Capital and Operations stakeholders, business analysts, functional owners, solution architects, developers, and technical teams to support complex incidents, service requests, operational initiatives, quarterly releases, and ongoing system maintenance. Your ability to troubleshoot complex functional issues, perform root cause analysis, provide expert functional guidance, optimize Oracle Fusion HCM solutions, and collaborate across functional and technical teams will directly contribute to service quality, operational stability, user satisfaction, and the continuous improvement of Oracle HCM capabilities.








**Your day\-to\-day**
* Lead the functional resolution of complex Oracle Fusion HCM incidents, service requests, and problem management activities;
* Analyze, troubleshoot, and resolve complex functional issues, perform root cause analysis, and identify recurring issues impacting system performance, operational stability, and user experience;
* Partner with Human Capital stakeholders to understand operational challenges, facilitate issue resolution discussions, and recommend sustainable solutions and process improvements;
* Configure, maintain, support, and optimize Oracle Fusion HCM solutions across Core HR, Workforce Structures, Position Management, Talent Management, Goal Management, Performance Management, Compensation, Recruiting, Benefits, Journeys, and Dynamic Skills, as well as Compensation processes, including Salary Review and Variable Pay;
* Support Talent Management capabilities, including Career Development, Succession Modeling, and Talent Review, as well as Compensation processes, including Salary Review and Variable Pay;
* Ensure strong functional integration between Oracle Fusion HCM and related Oracle solutions, including ERP Financials, Project Portfolio Management (PPM), Identity and Security Frameworks, and Reporting and Analytics platforms;
* Participate in support governance activities, backlog reviews, release readiness assessments, and prioritization discussions, while assessing the impacts of Oracle quarterly updates, new functionality, and system enhancements;
* Participate in testing and validation activities related to fixes, patches, quarterly updates, and enhancements, and validate proposed solutions prior to deployment;
* Produce and maintain functional documentation, troubleshooting guides, knowledge articles, support playbooks, and operational standards, while promoting knowledge sharing and mentoring Functional Analysts and junior team members;
* Collaborate with stakeholders, Solution Architects, Technical Leads, Developers, Functional Owners, and other CoE colleagues to support operational excellence, system optimization, service quality, and continuous improvement initiatives.






**Keys to your success**
* Minimum 6\-10 years of experience as a Functional Analyst working with Oracle packaged solutions, including 4\-7 years of hands\-on experience with Oracle Fusion Cloud HCM;
* Demonstrated experience supporting complex Oracle Fusion HCM environments and production support activities;
* Experience supporting complex cross\-functional and integrated business processes in global Oracle Fusion HCM environments;
* Experience participating in Oracle quarterly release assessments and testing activities, while driving process improvements and system optimization initiatives;
* Experience documenting functional solutions and operational procedures, and contributing to knowledge development within a support organization;
* Experience working within a Center of Excellence (CoE) operating model and mentoring analysts or junior team members;
* Strong analytical, communication, stakeholder management, collaboration, coaching, and organizational skills, with the ability to influence decision\-making, manage competing priorities, and balance strategic thinking with hands\-on functional execution.


**Extra edge**
* Oracle Fusion HCM certification;
* Experience working within ITIL\-based support environments, with service requests, incidents, problem management processes, and Oracle quarterly update planning, testing, and deployment activities;
* Experience with OTBI, BI Publisher, Power BI, or Power Query, as well as experience supporting enterprise\-wide Oracle HCM transformation, stabilization, or continuous improvement initiatives;
* Understanding of integrations, data conversions, data governance, and data quality processes, knowledge of HR compliance, employee data governance, and audit requirements, and advanced Microsoft Excel skills;
* French skills.


**Language Skills**
* English: Proficient






